<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan raises rates on dollar certificates.</title>
<headline>Pakistan raises rates on dollar certificates.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said Wednesday it had raised interest rates on five-year maturity dollar bearer certificates for May but kept rates for similar other foreign currency certificates unchanged:  Currency	     May 1-31	     April 1-30</p>
<p> U.S. dollar	  9.25		   9.00 percent P.A.</p>
<p> Pound sterling     9.75		   9.75 percent P.A.</p>
<p> Deutsche mark	7.25		   7.25 percent P.A.</p>
<p> Japanese yen	 4.00		   4,00 percent P.A.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
